<title>USA: US Senate FY 98 ag funds bill caps EEP at $150 Mln.</title>
<headline>US Senate FY 98 ag funds bill caps EEP at $150 Mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Senate passed a $50.7 billion fiscal 1998 funding bill for the Agriculture Department and related agencies on Thursday, including a $150 million cap on the major U.S. ag export subsidy plan.</p>
<p>The Clinton administration requested $500 million for the Export Enhancement Program but did not mention the matter in a statement distributed three hours before the vote.</p>
<p>The House began debate last week on its version of the bill but has not completed work. Its bill proposed $205 million for EEP.</p>
</text>
